          "worked": "The branches meet at $(-2,3)$ and $(1,3)$.\n\nDraw $y=3$ between these points. Extend $y=-2x-1$ to the left through $(-3,5)$, and extend $y=2x+1$ to the right through $(2,5)$. Both joins are included and there are no gaps. The $y$-intercept is $(0,3)$.",
